# Before we talk about code, let's clarify some of your terminology usage...

# The fundamental difference between a list and a tuple is this:

# A list is mutable, meaning its values can be changed after creation.
# A tuple is immutable, meaning its values cannot be changed after creation.

# The matrix variable is a list of other list objects. This is how we can get Python to give us behavior similar to a 2-D array in other languages like C/C++ and Java*.

# * As an aside... C used to be the first programming language students would learn in traditional 4-year Computer Science programs, because it makes it easier to understand what is actually going on under the hood of other languages like Python (The runtime engine of which is written in Java) and JavaScript (which is written in C++). 🙃

